The main goal of this project is to help beginners understand algorithms, data structures, and connectionist artificial intelligence.

By the end of this project, students should be able to:

• Explain what algorithms are and how they solve problems.
• Understand basic searching and sorting algorithms.
• Identify common data structures and explain their purposes.
• Describe the basic components of neural networks, including neurons, layers, and weights.
• Explain how neural networks learn from training data.
• Understand the relationship between algorithms, data structures, and connectionist AI.
• Recognize real-world applications of these concepts.

References:

1. ACM Computer Science Learning Objectives
https://ccecc.acm.org/guidance/computer-science/objectives/
2. Microsoft Learn — A Guide to Artificial Intelligence
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/a-guide-to-artificial-intelligence/
